<title>CANADA: Hydro-Quebec names interim chairman.</title>
<headline>Hydro-Quebec names interim chairman.</headline>
<dateline>QUEBEC CITY 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Quebec government said on Wednesday it named Jean-Andre Elie as interim chairman of Hydro-Quebec, the provincially owned electricity utility.</p>
<p>The announcement followed the forced resignation on Tuesday night of Yvon Martineau, chairman since March 22, 1995. Martineau's departure was widely expected because of executive infighting and a power struggle involving provincial Energy Minister Guy Chevrette.</p>
<p>He was the second senior executive to resign from the utility in two months. President and chief executive Benoit Michel quit in July over disagreements with Martineau.</p>
<p>Elie, 52, a businessman, has been a member of Hydro-Quebec's board since 1987.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100</p>
